From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:54:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] atbm6031: transfer in 488-byte SDIO blocks

The stock 613x driver runs the 6031-X's function at a 488-byte block: a
1.6 KB frame takes 4 blocks instead of 7. wsm_buf_reserve() rounded with
a power-of-two mask, and a wrong one; round up instead.
---
 hal_apollo/bh.h  | 2 +-
 hal_apollo/wsm.c | 5 +----
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hal_apollo/bh.h b/hal_apollo/bh.h
index 41f1e7f..60f4e58 100644
--- a/hal_apollo/bh.h
+++ b/hal_apollo/bh.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 /* extern */ struct atbm_common;
 
-#define SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE 256
+#define SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE 488
 
 /* Suspend state privates */
 enum atbm_bh_pm_state {
diff --git a/hal_apollo/wsm.c b/hal_apollo/wsm.c
index a907023..13a1893 100644
--- a/hal_apollo/wsm.c
+++ b/hal_apollo/wsm.c
@@ -3388,10 +3388,7 @@ static int wsm_buf_reserve(struct wsm_buf *buf, size_t extra_size)
 	size_t pos = buf->data - buf->begin;
 	size_t size = pos + extra_size;
 
-	if (size & (SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE - 1)) {
-		size &= SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE;
-		size += SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE;
-	}
+	size = roundup(size, SDIO_BLOCK_SIZE);
 
 	buf->begin = atbm_krealloc(buf->begin, size, GFP_KERNEL | GFP_DMA);
 	if (buf->begin) {
-- 
